Subject: rcutils: take the XSI strerror_r branch on musl
Origin: DHI-internal (musl libc build of rcutils for the alpine leaf)
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/ros2/rcutils.git e014b89367050bba69a6a4cd6cab11fa99780adf
Verify: cmd `ros2 topic list` expect "/rosout"
Forwarded: no (musl is not a REP 2000 platform)
Drop-When: never: rcutils keys the GNU strerror_r branch on _GNU_SOURCE, which musl defines without the GNU variant

rcutils picks the GNU strerror_r, which returns char *, whenever _GNU_SOURCE is defined. musl defines _GNU_SOURCE but
only provides the XSI strerror_r, which returns int, so GCC rejects the assignment as an int to pointer conversion and
rcutils fails to compile. Requiring __GLIBC__ for the GNU branch sends musl to the XSI branch and leaves glibc builds
unchanged.

--- a/src/strerror.c
+++ b/src/strerror.c
@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@
 {
 #if defined(_WIN32)
   strerror_s(buffer, buffer_length, errno);
-#elif defined(_GNU_SOURCE) && (!defined(ANDROID) || __ANDROID_API__ >= 23) && !defined(__QNXNTO__)
+#elif defined(__GLIBC__) && defined(_GNU_SOURCE) && (!defined(ANDROID) || __ANDROID_API__ >= 23) && !defined(__QNXNTO__)
   /* GNU-specific */
   char * msg = strerror_r(errno, buffer, buffer_length);
   if (msg != buffer) {
